# nr-office-engine-author-actions: the author action of the office engine (module mixdog-office::author)

Written without cargo: nothing below has been compiled (the lead compiles the wave). The module is a library the Office tool's
dispatch (a later task of the office track: nr-office-engine-qa-finalize-dispatch) calls; this task registers no protocol method and
no service, so nothing is removed from SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs.

It needs these wires applied first (it calls what they add): nr-office-engine-open-create.wire (`pub mod create; mode; open;
working_copy;` in session/mod.rs, `mixdog_ooxml::portable`), nr-office-engine-snapshot.wire (`pub mod snapshot;`),
nr-office-engine-inspect.wire (`pub mod inline_audit; pub mod inspect;`), nr-office-engine-render.wire (`pub mod render;`),
nr-office-author-xlsx-build.wire (`pub mod xlsx_build; pub mod xlsx_html_runner;` in mixdog-office-author/src/lib.rs; the Excel route
calls `run_xlsx_html_authoring`), nr-office-author-pptx-build.wire (`pub mod pptx_build; pub mod pptx_html_runner;`, already in lib.rs
of the tree).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod snapshot;` (after `pub mod session;` if that one is not applied yet) add, and extend the crate documentation by one line
("[`author`] is the `author` action: a document written from HTML (or a pptxgenjs script), staged, gated, landed over its target and
opened as a session."):

    pub mod author;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml
[dependencies], keeping the list sorted. Each line may already be there from the earlier fragments of the track (render adds
mixdog-fonts, mixdog-office-author and tokio; open-create adds mixdog-pdf and mixdog-raster as dependencies): add each once. New with
this task:

    mixdog-core-api = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-fonts = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-office-author = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-pdf = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-raster = { workspace = true }

(`mixdog-fonts` and `mixdog-pdf` are [dev-dependencies] lines in the snapshot fragment: make them [dependencies] lines and keep the
dev-dependency lines only where they carry a feature. `mixdog-core-api` is the crate of `domain::ext::BrowserEndpoint`, which
`SystemAuthor` holds; `mixdog-raster` is the crate of `SvgFonts` and of the comparison image. None of them depends on mixdog-office,
so there is no cycle. All are [workspace.dependencies] entries and members already; no external crate enters the lock.)
The test `tests/twin_author.rs` uses `mixdog-office-base` with `test-support`, `mixdog-rt`, `tempfile`, `tokio` (feature rt), `mixdog-fsio`,
`mixdog-js` and `serde_json`, all in the manifest already.

